WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:06.431
Insects have long been a staple food in Asia..
in Europe, not so much.

00:00:06.431 --> 00:00:08.800
But diets are changing, with ever more people
trying to avoid meat – for health or moral

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.460
reasons, or because raising farm animals is
less and less sustainable.

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:19.160
Today, the European Commission has officially
declared mealworms to be food.. it’s a game

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.949
changer for insect farmers, many of whom have
so far operated under temporary license.

00:00:22.949 --> 00:00:28.070
They are now hoping to grow their business
and for YOU to eat mealworms every once in

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:29.659
a while.. as just another source of protein.

00:00:29.659 --> 00:00:36.710
Our reporter Lars Halter went to one of Germany’s
largest insect farms.. he sent us this report.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:42.590
Schnürpflingen.. a little town in Southern
Germany, not far from where the Danube river

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:47.740
starts its long journey East.. there’s a
small church, and fields as far as the eye

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.640
can see.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:56.280
And here is where you can catch a glimpse
of the future of our food.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.120
And these guys have nothing to do with it.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:06.230
No, we're looking at another source of protein..
and it's coming from this rather nondescript

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:12.350
place: two huge factory buildings.. the farm
is called Six Feet to Eat... and they’re

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.570
raising mealworms here.

00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:26.790
These tiny insects, just over 2 centimeters
long, could be key to feeding the planet.

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:31.760
Insects are rich in protein.. up to 70 percent
of their entire mass in protein.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:38.990
In addition to that, they're also rich in
healthy Omega-3 fatty acids.. like fish..

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:46.410
except with fish you have a 2 percent share
of Omega-3 fatty acids, and some insects,

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:56.700
especially the mealworm, have over 14 percent..
that's seven times as much.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:02.450
Literally millions of insects are being raised
here.. mealworms, crickets, grasshoppers...

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:09.300
each breed with very particular needs... like
steady temperatures of up to 40 degrees.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:14.360
The insects live for just four to five weeks..
before they make their way into a fridge,

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:18.140
fall into a deep sleep that ends in a roasting
oven.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:23.790
They’re packaged… and sent to stores,
restaurants or straight to consumers.. who

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.709
are currently paying premium for the product.

00:02:26.709 --> 00:02:32.080
But with the EU paving the way, the company
hopes to produce cheaper soon.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:40.041
There are some insects that are ideally suited
for ethical factory farming.. like the mealworm

00:02:40.041 --> 00:02:41.340
or the cricket.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:45.340
We're currently establishing some level of
automation in our processes to get away from

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.709
a lot of the manual labor that's currently
needed.

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:57.209
That is a way to cut cost and it will help
bring consumer prices down, too.

00:02:57.209 --> 00:03:01.690
But what about those who can’t stomach a
bug on their salad or pasta dish?

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:03.650
Well, they can go to the Nürnbäcker.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:09.160
Kurt Heinlein is a baker in Nürnberg and
he has been specializing in interesting ingredients..

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.840
like spelt.. or, well, insects.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:18.660
His insect bread contains 20 percent mealworm
flower.. it's pricey.. at over 8 Euro for

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:29.560
a small loaf.. but customers have quickly
taken an interest.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:34.239
We were positively surprised.. especially
with regards to our older customers.

00:03:34.239 --> 00:03:38.390
We thought that the younger generation would
be more likely to try out something new..

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:43.709
but in fact it was the over-fifty group that
got really excited about it.. and many even

00:03:43.709 --> 00:03:48.980
tried the whole mealworms, too

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:54.120
Reason enough for the baker to hope that his
store stays busy.. and customers are enjoying

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.709
more of his experiments.

